  "notes": "Decoder only (the encoder is not used for generation). z ~ N(0, I), styles cycled. Outputs hit probability, velocity, offset per cell. Core ML packages are fp16. SURPRISE: the mlx_gpu fp32 reference is itself not fp32-exact at b=2000. MLX 0.32.4 GPU fp32 matmul with >= 8 rows has TF32-class error (probe: 512-term sums of N(0,1) entries, max err 0.07-0.09 vs fp64 for M = 8..2000, 1e-5 at M = 1; mlx_cpu and numpy 1e-4). So numpy/mlx_cpu disagree with mlx_gpu on 1.25% of threshold patterns while matching an fp64 decode 100%, and mlx_gpu matches fp64 on 98.75%. qualifies() still judges against mlx_gpu as pre-registered; task has *_vs_fp64 fields for the exact comparison."
 },
